      "html": "<ul><li>Origin: Colombia / Venezuela</li><li>Available size: 6-8 cm</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/uaru-fernandezyepezi/",
      "html": "<p>The home of this extremely rare cichlid is in the border area of Colombia and Venezuela, where it occurs in the area of the Rio Atabapo.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/uaru-fernandezyepezi/",
      "html": "<p>Their requirements are similar to those of the Altum angels: the water hardness should be low, the temperature high (around 29°C) and the pH value significantly in the acidic range. High temperatures and a low germ count improve the environment.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/uaru-fernandezyepezi/",
      "html": "<p>For the first time, some offspring of Uaru fernandezyepezi were offered (April 2008). From the same region come other challenging fishes such as the Altum angels.</p>"
    }
  ],
